course: dictionary
lesson: 15699
title: Tongs: a tool and a phrase
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words name a tool you can see and touch. Context tells you what the tool is for. «Dad used tongs to turn the sausages on the barbecue.» Turning sausages is a cooking job, and you need something to hold them. The picture of the barbecue tells you tongs are a kitchen tool.
explain: Look at what the tongs do. «Use the tongs to lift the salad onto the plates.» and «The scientist used tongs to lift the hot dish out of the flame.» In both sentences, the tongs pick up and hold things that could burn your hands. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence to check it.
explain: Some words belong to a phrase, and the phrase means something different from its single words. «The two brothers argued hammer and tongs about who should wash up.» Hammer and tongs are not tools in this sentence. The words argued and noisily around it show that it means arguing with great energy.
fact: Tongs is a noun for a tool with two long arms joined at one end.
fact: Tongs is plural, so we say «a pair of tongs» or «these tongs».
fact: «Tongs» are used to pick up and hold things such as food on a barbecue, salad, ice cubes or hot coals.
fact: Science tongs, also called crucible tongs, hold hot things in the lab.
fact: «Hammer and tongs» means with great energy, often noisily arguing.
exercise: «Dad used tongs to turn the sausages on the barbecue.» What are the tongs used for here? | Playing a tune | Cutting bread into slices | Watering the garden | *Holding and turning hot food
exercise: «The scientist used tongs to lift the hot dish out of the flame.» Why did she use tongs? | To make the dish heavier | *To keep her hands away from the heat | To tell the time | To play a game with the flame
exercise: «The two brothers argued hammer and tongs about who should wash up.» What does hammer and tongs mean? | Using a hammer to fix the sink | Quietly agreeing with each other | Holding things very gently | *With great energy, often noisily arguing
test: Which of these is a pair of tongs most likely used for? | Sleeping in a bed | Painting a fence | *Picking up ice cubes | Writing a letter
test: Find the word in «Use the tongs to lift the salad onto the plates» that names the tool. | plates | lift | salad | *tongs
exam: In «The two brothers argued hammer and tongs», what does hammer and tongs mean? | Working very slowly and carefully | Two tools joined at one end | Holding hot things in a lab | *With great energy, often noisily arguing
